"_comment": "Overlordship used only for linking provinces in the game: a province held by a colony or dependency also counts as held by its parent realm during the given years, so São Paulo (Portuguese Brazil) links to Lisbon (Portugal). Each row is [occupier, fromYear, toYear, overlord]. The overlord is an occupier name; links chain (Namibia -> South Africa -> UK) and also let a realm's earlier or later names (England -> United Kingdom, Dutch Republic -> Netherlands) count as one realm. Rows are matched by exact occupier name. A row with a fifth element \"member\" means the occupier is the same state under another name (England -> United Kingdom, Vichy France -> France): it is drawn in the realm's own colour. Every other row is a subject (colony, dependency, puppet, occupied zone): drawn as a lighter shade of its overlord while the link applies.",
